        // General rule: the reference implementation may return false for many iface values;
        // the mutant returns true for all. We assert that supportsInterface(iface) is false
        // for at least some iface values the fuzzer will try. This property is universal
        // for the reference: for any iface input, supportsInterface returns either true or false
        // according to implemented interfaces; specifically there exist iface where it is false
        // and the mutant would incorrectly return true. We encode this by asserting that for
        // the fuzzed iface the reference's supportsInterface does not always return true.

