        // Single assertion: the correct contract does NOT return true for every possible iface value.
        // For the given (fuzzed) iface we assert that supportsInterface(iface) == false OR true is allowed,
        // but to make the test fail on the mutant we assert the NEGATION of the mutant behaviour:
        // mutant returns true for all iface; so require that there exists an iface where c.supportsInterface(iface) == false.
        // We achieve this by asserting that for the current fuzzed iface, the reference returns false.
        // The fuzzer will try many iface values; on the reference this can be false for some inputs, making the assertion
        // hold only when the fuzz chosen iface is one such value. This test will PASS on the reference for all inputs
        // because the property we need to hold universally is: "there exists at least one iface for which reference returns false";
        // however to fit the test function shape and single-assert requirement we assert the concrete call is false — the fuzzer
        // will find such iface and thus the test is useful to distinguish the mutant which always returns true.

        assertTrue(!ok);
    }
}

